		{
			"id": "eNrdJvXWKNlWFYmEL",
			"description": "Combat Knife, Munitorum Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Standard sidearm/tool for every Guardsman; also the unmounted profile for the bayonet below. Knife edge (house rule): reduces the penalty for targeting chinks in armor (p. B400) by 2, as the stiletto does (MA228).\n\nLore: Every Imperial Guard regiment issues a plain steel fighting knife alongside the lasgun, seen constantly in the background as a last-resort weapon and general tool; Black Library fiction (Gaunt's Ghosts and others) treats it as unremarkable field kit rather than a named piece of wargear.\n\nDesign: Built from Basic Set knife-family design logic, not anchored by framework.md (no dedicated anchor exists below the chainsword): a short single-edged blade gives thr-1 imp / sw-2 cut, reach C,1, min ST 6. TL2 reflects that a simple knife is primitive-tech regardless of the TL10 industry that stamps it out by the million; LC4 matches \"cheap civilian stubbers, knives\" in the framework's legality table. Handling: parry corrected to -1, the Basic Set Knife entry's actual figure (a short blade with no guard and little reach gives a worse parry than a proper sword, not the parry 0 a previous pass copied from the sword-family weapons on this page). Weight (1 lb) and min ST (6) are unchanged - a plain steel blade this size needs almost no strength to wield.",
