		{
			"id": "eU_vgMKA7GqYcPGFI",
			"description": "Bayonet, Lug-Mounted",
			"local_notes": "Fits the standard-issue lasgun's bayonet lug (and most stub-pattern long arms of similar profile); mounting or removing it takes a Ready maneuver. Mounted, treat it as an improvised short spear rather than a knife for reach and defaults. Knife edge (house rule): reduces the penalty for targeting chinks in armor (p. B400) by 2, as the stiletto does (MA228).\n\nLore: Depicted throughout Guard fiction as the last line of defence when a firefight closes to melee and a Guardsman's lasgun runs dry or jams - \"fix bayonets\" is a recurring line in Astra Militarum combat scenes, most famously associated with charge orders in Gaunt's Ghosts-style trench and siege fighting.\n\nDesign: Same blade and knife-mode profile as the Munitorum combat knife above; the mounted profile follows Basic Set convention for a bayonet fixed to a long arm (treated as a short thrusting spear once fixed, reach 1,2, +1 to thrust damage for the leverage of the gun's length behind the point) rather than inventing new mechanics. TL/LC as the knife it's built from. Handling: unmounted knife-mode parry corrected to -1 to match the Munitorum knife it shares a blade with; the mounted (Spear-skill) profile keeps parry 0, the Basic Set figure for a one-handed spear braced on a long arm, since a fixed bayonet has more reach and leverage to block with than a bare knife does. Weight and min ST are unchanged.",
