		{
			"id": "eotvmedYqeXwA0tD_",
			"description": "Entrenching Tool, Folding",
			"local_notes": "Doubles as a digging tool; treat as an improvised weapon (already priced and statted as one, no further penalty needed when it's used as intended). The U means the wielder cannot parry again with it until a turn has passed since the last parry (B404) - a heavy, head-forward tool is slow to bring back on guard.\n\nLore: Standard Guard field-engineering kit, folded and slung on webbing; depicted in trench-warfare-flavoured Guard fiction being swung in desperate close combat as often as it's used to dig in, in the tradition of real-world entrenching-tool improvised weapons.\n\nDesign: Not anchored; built as a short, heavy-headed improvised axe/mace per Basic Set logic - a folding steel spade has enough mass to crush but a poor edge and balance, giving sw+1 cr, reach 1, min ST 8. TL5 reflects the folding steel tool itself (an industrial product), not the Imperium's overall manufacturing TL. Handling: parry corrected to -1U, the Basic Set convention for a head-heavy chopping/crushing tool (Axe/Mace family, B271): it is worse to parry with than a purpose-built one-handed weapon, and swinging a lopsided spade-head leaves it out of position to parry again right away. Weight (5 lb) and min ST (8) are unchanged.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
			"tech_level": "5",
			"legality_class": "4",
			"base_value": "30",
			"base_weight": "5 lb",
			"weapons": [
