		{
			"id": "e-SAiCWqf0WZCgFDT",
			"description": "Maul, Guardsman's Club",
			"local_notes": "Riot batons, Arbites-issue billy clubs and improvised trench clubs all use this profile. The U means the wielder cannot parry again with it until a turn has passed since the last parry.\n\nLore: The plainest possible melee weapon: a weighted length of wood, plas or scavenged pipe, seen everywhere from hive underworld gangs to penal-legion improvisation in Guard-adjacent fiction; no source treats it as anything but a crude, universally available last resort.\n\nDesign: Straight Basic Set club design (sw+2 cr, reach 1, min ST 9); not anchored by framework.md since it sits well below the chainsword tier, TL0 because a club needs no technology at all. Handling: parry corrected to -1U, the standard Basic Set figure for a simple blunt club (Axe/Mace family) rather than the parry 0 a sword or knife gets - a plain weighted stick has no guard to block with and is slow to recover a swing. Weight and min ST are unchanged.",
