		{
			"id": "eFa-JAccJLKXQIK28",
			"description": "Catachan Fang",
			"local_notes": "Doubles as a survival/jungle tool as well as a sidearm; several Catachan-pattern variants exist, all statted the same. Knife edge (house rule): reduces the penalty for targeting chinks in armor (p. B400) by 2, as the stiletto does (MA228).\n\nLore: The heavy-bladed survival knife/machete carried by Catachan Jungle Fighters and often imitated by other jungle- and feral-world regiments; depicted in Astra Militarum background material as a point of regimental pride and a genuinely effective close-combat weapon rather than a mere tool, distinguishing it from the standard Munitorum knife.\n\nDesign: One step up from the Munitorum combat knife on the knife-to-machete continuum: a heavy blade in the Basic Set Large Knife class, scaled up to thr+1 imp, sw cut, reach C,1, min ST 8 and 2.5 lb (the combat knife is thr-1/sw-2 at 1 lb). It stays a Knife-skill weapon with the Knife parry of -1, so it is clearly a different item from the sabre. Not a framework anchor; calibrated between the knife above and the chainsword anchor below.",
