		{
			"id": "eHI8dVy_uJsN79tMA",
			"description": "Commissar's Sabre",
			"local_notes": "A badge of office as much as a weapon; carrying one marks the bearer as a commissar or officer to friend and foe alike.\n\nLore: The curved sabre is near-universal Commissariat and senior-officer iconography in Astra Militarum art and fiction, frequently drawn during summary executions or to lead a charge (Ciaphas Cain and Gaunt's Ghosts both use this image repeatedly); it is functional, not purely ceremonial, and commissars are shown killing with it.\n\nDesign: A light sabre in the Broadsword class (Basic Set Cavalry Saber: sw+1 cut, thr+1 imp, parry 0, ST 10), at 2.5 lb, 0.5 lb under the Basic Set's 3 lb: a slimmer officer's blade. It is a rank symbol first and out-cuts nothing in a Guardsman's hands, so the profile is the plain baseline; the difference from a war-knife is in cost, finish and legal status. LC2 and a high cost reflect that carrying one signals officer or commissar rank rather than a mechanical edge. In the fiction commissars also carry chainswords and power swords, which are separate entries. Broadsword parry 0.",
