		{
			"id": "eVRfiQB-FE280ejDP",
			"description": "Chainsword",
			"local_notes": "The motor and chain-teeth tear rather than cleanly cut, hence the Armor Divisor (2) rather than a clean-edged blade's no-divisor cut; the framework anchor notes it \"skids off power armour\" - against DR 70+ targets a human wielder essentially never penetrates, at the table's discretion the GM may rule the chain simply fails to bite rather than dealing a grazing wound. A jammed or fouled chain (tangled cloth, bone, or a lucky parry) may stall the motor until cleared with a Ready maneuver.\n\nLore: The archetypal Imperial melee weapon: sergeants, veterans and officers across the Astra Militarum, plus most Chaos and Imperial cultist/human forces, carry a motorised chainblade; consistently shown butchering unarmoured infantry but failing to trouble power armour, matching the framework anchor's own description.\n\nDesign: Fixed anchor (Rescale): sw+2d(2) cut, reach 1, parry 0, min ST 10. The Rescale raised the chainsword from a flat sw+1d cut with no divisor to sw+2d(2). A Guardsman (ST 10-11, sw 1d to 1d+1) rolls about 3d(2), average 10.5-11.5: against carapace (DR 70, eff. 35) that never penetrates, and against a flak vest (DR 30, eff. 15) only about 5-9% of hits, so a Guardsman rarely gets through flak. An Astartes wielder (ST 30, sw 5d+2, so 7d+2(2), average 26.5) usually does: 99% against flak, 2.2% against carapace, and it skids off power armour (eff. DR 50+) outright. That matches the framework's \"tears flesh and flak; bites carapace; skids off power armour\", with \"tears flak\" belonging to the Marine. TL10 and LC2 per the framework's own worked example (\"Standard Imperial manufacture: TL10 ... chainsword\"). Handling: Broadsword's Basic Set parry (0) is correct for a bladed, guarded weapon like a chainsword, so no U or -1 correction applies (unlike the axe/mace/maul family). Weight (6 lb, heavier than a plain sword for the motor housing and chain loop) and min ST 10 (above a mundane broadsword's ST 10 only in mass) are the only free parameters. Monoedge rule (user direction): chain teeth are monomolecular-edged, so every chain weapon now takes armour divisor (3). A Guardsman's 3d(3) still only tears flak; a Marine's 7d+2(3) bites carapace on 74% of hits and a Mark VII neck seal on 86%, but gets through a power-armoured torso only 4% of the time.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
			"tech_level": "10",
			"legality_class": "2",
			"base_value": "600",
			"base_weight": "6 lb",
