		{
			"id": "eW1c2EhdKNjhsZPPE",
			"description": "Chainaxe",
			"local_notes": "Chain-vs-armour and jamming rules as the chainsword; the single heavy blade makes it even more prone to sticking in a solid hit than a chainsword's finer teeth. The U means the wielder cannot parry again with it until a turn has passed since the last parry.\n\nLore: A heavier chain weapon favoured by close-combat specialists and several Chapters and warband traditions (most infamously World Eaters iconography, though Loyalist Astartes and some Guard veteran/ penal formations field it too); depicted as hitting harder but handling clumsier than a chainsword.\n\nDesign: Scaled from the chainsword anchor the way Basic Set/Low-Tech scale a one-handed axe over a one-handed sword of the same era: a single heavy, chain-driven axe-head carries more mass into the swing than a chainsword's full-length blade, for +2 damage over the chainsword's sw+2d, keeping the same Armor Divisor (2) since it is the same grinding chain-teeth mechanic. At Astartes ST (sw 5d+2, so 7d+4(2), average 28.5) an axe swing bites carapace (DR 70, eff. 35) on 6.1% of hits, against the Astartes chainsword's 2.2%: roughly three times as often, though neither reliably bites carapace, and both skid off power armour. That matches its \"hits harder but handles clumsier\" reputation. Min ST 16 sits just above the Astartes chainsword's ST 15 because the axe is a bit heavier (15 lb vs. 14 lb). It is an Astartes weapon: an unusually strong or augmented human can swing it one-handed only at a stiff penalty for the missing strength. Handling: parry -1U, the Basic Set Axe/Mace figure for a one-handed axe (worse than a sword's parry 0, and unready after a parry the way every axe/mace/maul weapon here reads). Monoedge rule (user direction): armour divisor (2) to (3). At ST 30 (7d+4(3)) it bites carapace on 86% of hits, a Mark VII neck seal on 94% and a Mark VII torso on 9%.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
			"tech_level": "10",
			"legality_class": "1",
			"base_value": "1400",
			"base_weight": "15 lb",
			"weapons": [
