		{
			"id": "e514r1ImDg5Gsn-Ka",
			"description": "Eviscerator",
			"local_notes": "Always wielded two-handed; the U means the wielder cannot parry again with it until a turn has passed since the last parry - the chain bucks hard enough in a solid hit to need a beat to bring back on guard, not merely a GM's-discretion \"treat as unready\" note. Sisters Repentia below the listed min ST take the normal reduced-ST penalties to skill rather than being unable to lift it - their fervour, not raw strength, is what the fiction credits.\n\nLore: An oversized, double-handed chain weapon issued to Adepta Sororitas Repentia squads doing penance in battle; consistently drawn and described as a huge, brutal chainblade too large and heavy for ordinary one-handed use, swung by zealots who accept the personal risk of wielding something this unwieldy.\n\nDesign: One further step up the chain-weapon family from the chainaxe: a two-handed weapon gets Basic Set's two-handed bonus over a one-handed weapon of the same family (roughly +1 die over the one-handed chainaxe's sw+2d+2, rounded to a clean sw+3d cut), keeping the shared chain-family Armor Divisor (2), with reach extended to 1,2. At a Sororitas-typical ST this still only scratches carapace occasionally and does nothing to power armour - fitting its role as an anti-personnel penance weapon, not an anti-Astartes one. Handling: re-derived against the real analogue of a Low-Tech two- handed greatsword-class weapon with a heavy chain drive bolted on - 25 lb loaded (well above a mundane two-handed sword's 6-8 lb, for the motor, drive chain and reinforced haft) with min ST 15, well under the Astartes chainaxe's ST 16 for 15 lb because two hands share the load (and above the human chainsword's ST 10/6 lb), to reflect real mass, not raw Astartes strength - this stays a human (if enhanced-by-faith) weapon per its Sororitas lore, hence the notes on using it below min ST rather than simply barring human use outright. Parry corrected to -1U (Two-Handed Sword's baseline plus the same chain-weapon \"must recover\" logic used for the chainsword family), replacing the previous GM's-discretion note with an actual mechanical flag. Monoedge rule (user direction): armour divisor (2) to (3). At ST 30 (8d+2(3)) it gets through a Mark VII torso on 18% of hits.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adepta Sororitas"
			],
			"tech_level": "10",
			"legality_class": "1",
			"base_value": "1000",
			"base_weight": "25 lb",
