		{
			"id": "e-K1lh2RJjoVpgDVi",
			"description": "Chainfist",
			"local_notes": "Shares the power fist's servo-driven punch (see Power Fist below) but replaces the smooth crushing plates with a ring of high-speed chain teeth for gnawing through bulkheads, void-ship hulls and vehicle armour rather than just crushing flesh and ceramite; a hit that penetrates a vehicle's DR may be ruled to lodge the fist in the material, costing a Ready maneuver to wrench free (GM's discretion). Like the power fist, it is slow and clumsy in a defensive sense: -2 to parry, and it cannot be used to Feint.\n\nLore: A rarer, heavier variant of the power fist mounting a chainblade ring instead of a plain gauntlet, issued to Terminators, Dreadnoughts and boarding specialists for boarding actions and siege-breaching where cutting through armour plate or a bulkhead matters as much as punching through a body; consistently shown as slower and more specialised than a plain power fist.\n\nDesign: Same servo-fist chassis and damage logic as the Power Fist entry below (thr plus a large flat die bonus from the hydraulic mechanism, not a multiplier on the wielder's own thrust; see that entry's design note), with the same (10) disruption-field divisor every Imperial power weapon shares (framework.md, power-field rule). The die count is one step down (+7d vs. the power fist's +8d) because chain teeth trade some raw hitting power for penetration and add their own moving parts' weight and drag. At Astartes ST 30 (thr 3d, so thr+7d = 10d, average 35) it penetrates Terminator plate (eff. DR 20) 99.7% of the time, keeping it a credible boarding and breaching weapon even though it hits slightly softer than a plain power fist. With the field off it is a chain-toothed gauntlet at the mundane baseline of thr+1d cut, reach C and parry -2 like the field-on line. TL11 (advanced Imperial/rare, shares the power-field-adjacent servo technology) and LC1 (Astartes power-weapon-tier legality per the framework). Handling: unarmed-style Brawling punch, not a bladed/axe weapon, so the axe/mace \"U\" convention doesn't apply; the -2 parry encodes how slow and hard to reposition a fist- mounted chain ring is. Weight 45 lb and min ST 17 are Astartes-only figures consistent with the Power Fist below. Monoedge rule (user direction): the field-off chain line takes armour divisor (3), as every chain weapon.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
			"tech_level": "11",
			"legality_class": "1",
			"base_value": "5000",
			"base_weight": "45 lb",
			"weapons": [
