		{
			"id": "e8KLfStwMXe219d4r",
			"description": "Shock Maul",
			"local_notes": "Draws from a small power cell; good for many dozens of charged strikes before a recharge is needed. The U means the wielder cannot parry again with it until a turn has passed since the last parry.\n\nLore: The standard Adeptus Arbites and hive-enforcer riot weapon: a shock-charged baton meant to subdue rather than kill, ubiquitous in Arbites background material and Necromunda-adjacent underhive fiction as the tool of choice for crowd control and arrests.\n\nDesign: Built as a plain club (sw+1 cr, matching the Guardsman's maul one step up for its denser Arbites-grade construction) plus a Basic Set electrical-stun effect layered on top as a secondary rules note (HT-3 or stunned) rather than a new damage type, since GURPS models \"shocked and dazed but not much hurt\" through the Stun rule, not through raw damage. Rescale note: this weapon's raw damage is left unchanged, since it was never anchored to any armour DR figure - it's plain ST-scaled club damage, and its entire purpose (subduing a target, not penetrating armour) is carried by the Stun rule rather than by beating DR, so the armour-anchor rescale doesn't touch it. TL10 for the power cell and stun generator; LC2 (enforcer/Arbites- issue, not general military) per the framework's \"military-issue heavy weapons, carapace, hellguns\" LC2 bracket. Handling: parry corrected to -1U to match the Axe/Mace family convention used consistently on this page (a rigid club-shaped weapon is worse to parry with than a sword, and slower to recover). Weight (3 lb) and min ST (8) are unchanged.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Arbites"
			],
			"tech_level": "10",
			"legality_class": "2",
			"base_value": "150",
			"base_weight": "3 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
