		{
			"id": "egq1n9N0VhpvqR6Nn",
			"description": "Electro-flail",
			"local_notes": "A flail can parry, but the U means the wielder cannot parry again with it until a turn has passed since the last parry; other fighters parry a flail attack at -4 (B404). The head's momentum makes it awkward around allies at close range.\n\nLore: A heavier, multi-headed shock weapon seen in Ecclesiarchy penitent and some Arbites riot-control contexts, its swinging heads and crackling charge making it as much an instrument of intimidation as of subjugation; less common than the shock maul and depicted as harder to control.\n\nDesign: Standard Basic Set flail design logic (extra reach when extended, more damage than a rigid weapon of similar weight for the whipping strike) applied one step above the shock maul (sw+2 cr vs. sw+1 cr) since a multi-headed flail carries more striking mass, plus the same HT-3 stun note. As with the shock maul, raw damage is unaffected by the armour-DR rescale: this is a subdual weapon whose job is done by the Stun rule, not by beating DR. TL/LC match the shock maul's bracket. Handling: parry 0U, the Basic Set Flail and Morningstar figure (the Basic Set lists both at 0U; attacks made with a flail are parried at -4, B404). Weight 6 lb (a Basic Set Morningstar) and min ST 10.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Arbites"
			],
			"tech_level": "10",
			"legality_class": "2",
			"base_value": "250",
			"base_weight": "6 lb",
