		{
			"id": "epCwfuGncQZF5UkaL",
			"description": "Power Maul, Arbites Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Toggling between settings is a free action; Arbitrators are trained and expected to keep the weapon on suppression setting for routine enforcement and switch to lethal only against a genuine threat. The U means the wielder cannot parry again with it until a turn has passed since the last parry.\n\nLore: A dual-mode maul issued to senior Arbites Judges and Marshals: an Adeptus Arbites badge of office as much as the shock maul is a street enforcer's tool, and background material is explicit that it can be dialled from a stunning baton up to a lethal power weapon.\n\nDesign: Suppression setting is the same maul-plus-stun-note logic as the shock maul family above, one step heavier (sw+2 cr) for the denser Arbites-issue head; its damage is unaffected by the Rescale for the same reason as the mundane shock weapons. Lethal setting applies this file's general power-field rule (framework.md: field-on = mundane baseline +3d, Armor Divisor (10)): sw+2 cr (field off) becomes sw+3d+2(10) cr (field on) - the same +3d/(10) step used to build every other field-on/field-off pair in this file, keeping the Arbites maul consistent with the Chapter- and Sororitas-issue power weapons below it despite its different institutional owner. Handling: parry corrected to -1U on both settings, matching the Axe/Mace family convention (a maul head, powered or not, is still a blunt, head-forward weapon). Weight (5 lb) and min ST (10) are unchanged.",
			"tags": [
