		{
			"id": "eTTPv9gti26dDXF6d",
			"description": "Power Sword",
			"local_notes": "The disruption field is a toggle (free action); with the field off, this is an unremarkable, if beautifully made, one-handed sword. A depleted or damaged power cell disables the field the same way.\n\nLore: The classic officer's and veteran's duelling and battle blade of the Imperium, from Guard colonels to Astartes veteran sergeants and Inquisitors; consistently shown shearing through flak, flesh and even power armour where a plain sword or chainsword would just bounce or skid, matching the framework anchor's own description.\n\nDesign: Fixed anchor (Rescale): sw+3d+1(10) cut, reach 1, parry 0, min ST 10. This entry also establishes the general \"power field\" rule every other powered edged/blunt weapon in this file is built from (framework.md, power-field rule): comparing the anchor to a plain one-handed sword's Basic Set baseline (sw+1 cut for a broadsword- class blade) shows the field itself contributes exactly +3d damage and Armor Divisor (10) over the same weapon with the field off - the \"field off\" line above is that same sw+1 cut baseline, unchanged by the Rescale (a plain sword's mundane edge doesn't care what DR anchors moved). This is why the field-off usage is included explicitly: the framework says power field on/off must be modelled as separate weapon lines, and this file applies the same +3d/(10) delta to every bladed/mace power weapon below (thunder hammers get +6d and power fists thr+8d instead, per the framework's own breakdown), scaled from each weapon's own mundane baseline rather than re-deriving the anchor each time. Checked against the armour anchors: a Guardsman-strength blow (ST 11, sw=1d+1, so field-on totals 4d+2) penetrates carapace (DR 70, eff. 7) 99.6% of the time, Astartes power armour (DR 100, eff. 10) 94.6% of the time, and Terminator plate (DR 200, eff. 20) 9.7% of the time; an Astartes-strength blow (ST 30, sw=5d+2, field-on 8d+3) penetrates Astartes power armour always and Terminator plate (eff. DR 20) 98.6% of the time. This matches the framework's \"the disruption field shears power armour whoever holds it\" - even a human's power sword reliably beats another human's power armour. TL11 and LC1 per the framework's \"Advanced Imperial/rare\" and \"power weapons\" brackets. This is the human-scale power sword; see Power Sword, Astartes Pattern below for the heavier Chapter-armoury version built the same way the Astartes chainsword is built from the human one. Handling: Broadsword's Basic Set parry (0) applies unchanged - a guarded, edged weapon, not an axe/mace. Weight (4 lb) and min ST (10) match a real one-handed duelling sword.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
