		{
			"id": "efgkiIfMQdwM8ycJ6",
			"description": "Power Sword, Astartes Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Field toggle and depleted-cell rules as the human-scale power sword.\n\nLore: Chapter armouries maintain power swords scaled to a Marine's own grip and reach for veteran sergeants and officers who favour a blade over a chainsword; visually similar to a human duelling sword but unmistakably oversized in a Space Marine's gauntlet, in the same way Astartes chainswords and combat knives read as full-size weapons in a human's hands.\n\nDesign: Exactly the Power Sword anchor's damage formula, unchanged (sw+3d+1(10) cut field on / sw+1 cut field off) - per the framework's rule that \"sw\" resolves from the wielder's own ST, an Astartes swinging this blade already rolls far more dice than a human swinging the human-scale version (Marine sw=5d+2, field-on 8d+3, average 31, vs. a Guardsman's sw=1d+1, field-on 4d+2) without the weapon's own formula changing at all; it penetrates Astartes plate always and Terminator plate (eff. DR 20) 98.6% of the time, exactly the same relationship the Astartes Chainsword has to the human Chainsword. Handling: what does change, per the framework's instruction that human- and Astartes-scale versions of the same weapon type need different weight and min ST, is the housing: a heavier blade, hilt and power cell built for a gauntleted hand runs 9 lb (vs. the human pattern's 4 lb - roughly the same +5 lb jump the Astartes combat knife takes over the human one) and needs min ST 16 (vs. ST 10), putting it firmly out of an unaugmented human's reach the way the Astartes chainsword's ST 15 does. Parry stays 0 (Broadsword, unguarded by any axe/mace correction).",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
			"tech_level": "11",
			"legality_class": "1",
			"base_value": "6500",
			"base_weight": "9 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
