		{
			"id": "e47s7JsiF3XBs0bI_",
			"description": "Power Axe",
			"local_notes": "Field toggle and depleted-cell rules as the power sword. The U means the wielder cannot parry again with it until a turn has passed since the last parry.\n\nLore: A heavier power weapon favoured where a wielder wants more raw hitting power than a power sword at the cost of some finesse - recurring wargear for Astartes veterans and Guard officers with a taste for a bigger blade.\n\nDesign: Applies the power-field rule established under Power Sword (+3d damage, Armor Divisor (10), field on vs. off) to a plain axe's Basic Set baseline (sw+2 cut, per the same broadsword-vs-axe relationship used for the mundane weapons above) rather than to the power sword's own base line, since an axe and a sword are not the same mundane weapon with a field bolted on. This is the human-scale power axe; see Power Axe, Astartes Pattern below for the Chapter- armoury version. Handling: parry corrected to -1U on both settings, matching every other Axe/Mace-family weapon on this page (the previous plain -1 left out the \"unready after parrying\" half of the Basic Set axe penalty). Weight (6 lb) and min ST (12) are unchanged.",
