		{
			"id": "eoQqJOxO-ow1rzIvJ",
			"description": "Power Axe, Astartes Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Field toggle and depleted-cell rules as the power sword; parry U as the human-scale Power Axe.\n\nLore: Chapter- and warband-armoury power axes built to Astartes proportions - a heavier, more brutal counterpart to the Astartes power sword, favoured by the same close-combat specialists who'd otherwise carry a chainaxe, for when raw stopping power against a fellow Astartes matters more than reach.\n\nDesign: Same sw+3d+2(10) cut / sw+2 cut formula as the human-scale Power Axe, unchanged - an Astartes swinging it already rolls a much bigger sw than a human would, exactly as with the Astartes power sword above. Handling: heavier axe-head, haft and cell built for a gauntleted grip push weight to 13 lb (vs. the human pattern's 6 lb) and min ST to 18 (vs. ST 12) - a bigger jump than the power sword's human-to-Astartes step, matching how the mundane Chainaxe (15 lb/ST 16) already sits above the mundane Chainsword (6 lb/ST 10) by a wider margin than a sword needs. Parry stays -1U, the same Axe/Mace-family correction as every other axe on this page.",
