		{
			"id": "e2Cw2r_O9UaE6dp2G",
			"description": "Power Maul",
			"local_notes": "Field toggle and depleted-cell rules as the power sword; this is the general-issue pattern the Arbites power maul above is built from. The U means the wielder cannot parry again with it until a turn has passed since the last parry.\n\nLore: A power weapon built around a blunt head rather than an edge, issued to some Ministorum, Sororitas and Guard-officer wielders who favour crushing force; background material treats it as functionally equivalent to a power sword or axe, just blunt rather than edged.\n\nDesign: Same power-field rule as Power Sword and Power Axe (+3d, field on vs. off), applied to a plain mace's Basic Set baseline (sw+2 cr); the field still applies Armor Divisor (10) and damage type stays crushing rather than switching to cut, since the field disrupts and shears at the point of impact regardless of whether the striking surface is an edge or a flat head - the wound is still blunt trauma amplified by the field, matching 40k depictions of power mauls caving in what they hit rather than slicing it. Handling: parry corrected to -1U on both settings, the same Axe/Mace convention as the Arbites power maul it's built from. Weight (5 lb) and min ST (11) are unchanged.",
