		{
			"id": "ecMFdBCvtbqJwR6uK",
			"description": "Crozius Arcanum",
			"local_notes": "Field toggle and depleted-cell rules as the power sword. The U means the wielder cannot parry again with it until a turn has passed since the last parry. Chapter Chaplains carry it with a Rosarius (see Force Fields), and its skull-topped head is an icon of their office.\n\nLore: The Chaplain's staff of office and power weapon: an ornate mace-like crozius with a power-field head, carried by Astartes Chaplains across Codex Space Marines background and Black Library Space Marine fiction. The Reclusiarch and Chaplains of most Chapters wield one as both weapon and holy symbol.\n\nDesign: The Astartes power mace, built on the power-field rule (+3d over the mundane weapon, armour divisor (10), field on vs. off) but from a heavier mundane baseline than the human Power Maul (sw+3 cr rather than sw+2 cr), as a two-hand-sized Astartes head on a one-hand haft. At Astartes ST 30 (sw 5d+2) it is 8d+5(10), average 33, penetrating Astartes plate always and Terminator plate (eff. DR 20) 99.6% of the time. Handling: 12 lb and min ST 16 sit between the Astartes Power Sword (9 lb/ST 16) and Power Axe (13 lb/ST 18); parry -1U, the Axe/Mace convention. TL11 and LC1 as every Astartes power weapon; priced $9,000 for the holy-relic rarity.",
