		{
			"id": "eBltyt28dyV1HcMUa",
			"description": "Relic Blade",
			"local_notes": "Always a unique, named heirloom weapon in the fiction; a given relic blade may carry additional individual traits or a name-specific ability a GM adds on top of this baseline profile.\n\nLore: Ancient, master-crafted power swords carried by Chapter Masters and other Astartes heroes, oversized compared to a standard power sword and wielded one-handed only by Astartes-grade strength; a recurring \"hero weapon\" across Black Library Space Marine fiction (e.g. named blades carried by Chapter Masters and First Company veterans).\n\nDesign: Applies the power-field rule (+3d, field on vs. off) to a two-handed greatsword's Basic Set baseline (sw+3 cut) rather than the one-handed broadsword baseline used for the standard power sword, reflecting a longer, heavier blade. At Astartes ST 30 (sw 5d+2, field-on 8d+5, average 33) it penetrates Astartes power armour (DR 100, eff. 10) always and Terminator plate (DR 200, eff. 20) 99.6% of the time, a step above the standard Astartes power sword's 98.6%, fitting its \"hero weapon\" status. Reach 1: wielded one-handed by an Astartes, so it does not take the two-handed greatsword's reach 1,2. Handling: re-derived against a real Low-Tech greatsword analogue (typically 6-8 lb at ST 14-15) scaled up for an oversized, master- crafted Astartes blade wielded one-handed: weight bumped from 8 lb to 10 lb and min ST from 16 to 17, keeping it a firmly Astartes-only weapon - a human could not meet the strength requirement even one-handed, matching the fiction that ordinary humans do not wield relic blades. Parry stays 0 (Broadsword, a guarded blade rather than an axe/mace weapon).",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
