		{
			"id": "eGSP4vxvePIoruuOW",
			"description": "Thunder Hammer",
			"local_notes": "Any hit that penetrates the target's DR also inflicts Knockback (B378) using the raw crushing damage rolled, even against a target too armoured to actually be wounded much - representing Astartes, Terminators and even light vehicles being physically hurled by the blow, per the weapon's fiction reputation. The 0U parry is the Basic Set figure for a two-handed maul/great axe class weapon (B271): it can still parry, but the wielder cannot parry again with it until a turn has passed since the last parry.\n\nLore: A massive two-handed maul carrying a huge capacitor coil, issued to Astartes Terminator assault squads and veteran sergeants; consistently shown caving in Terminator armour and knocking opponents flying rather than cutting them, distinct in style from the disruption-field swords and axes above.\n\nDesign: Fixed anchor (Rescale, framework.md): sw+6d(10) cr. A two-handed great maul's Basic Set baseline is sw+3 cr (unchanged, field off); the field's bonus is scaled up well past the standard +3d used for the sword/axe/maul family (framework.md: \"thunder hammers +6d\") since a thunder hammer's coil is built into a much larger head than a sword's blade, with the shared (10) disruption-field divisor. An earlier draft used (3) on the theory that a hammer beats armour by concussion, but that left a Marine's average blow unable to clear Terminator armour, contradicting the hammer's role as the Terminator-killer. At Astartes ST 30 (sw 5d+2, so 11d+2, average 40.5) against the Rescale's Terminator anchor (DR 200, eff. 20) it penetrates every time and adds knockback. The knockback note captures the anchor-adjacent \"thunder hammer\" lore detail (send Marines and even light vehicles flying) using the existing Basic Set B378 knockback rule rather than a new mechanic, per this project's preference for built, not borrowed, but standard-rules design. Handling: re-derived against a real Low-Tech great maul analogue (Great Maul: roughly 15-20 lb, ST 17-19, two-handed) scaled up hard for a \"massive two-handed maul carrying a huge capacitor coil\" - weight bumped from a previously-copied 35 lb to 40 lb and min ST from 15 to 21, both far above the standard power sword/axe/maul family (ST 10-12) and above even the Astartes chainaxe (ST 16), matching the lore's \"heaviest thing an Astartes swings\" reputation. Parry is corrected from a flat -1 to 0U, the actual Basic Set two-handed axe/mace figure: it is not worse to parry with than a one-handed weapon (0, not -1), but it is unbalanced and needs a turn to recover before parrying again (U) - previously this weapon had neither the right parry value nor the U flag.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
			"tech_level": "11",
			"legality_class": "1",
			"base_value": "9000",
			"base_weight": "40 lb",
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "wzBOOiH3slY1ZzcV-",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "cr",
						"st": "sw",
						"base": "6d",
						"armor_divisor": 10
					},
					"reach": "1",
					"parry": "0U",
					"strength": "21",
					"usage": "Field on, two-handed swing",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "dx",
							"modifier": -5
						},
						{
							"type": "skill",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Two-Handed Axe/Mace"
