		{
			"id": "eKyu2ZkrhO81GRIPk",
			"description": "Lightning Claws, Paired",
			"local_notes": "One claw worn per hand; each claw is identical to the single Lightning Claw above. A wielder trained in two-weapon fighting may attack with both in the same turn using the standard Basic Set rules for fighting with two weapons (dual-weapon attack/off-hand weapon training), rather than any bespoke \"paired claws\" rule - this file adds no new mechanic for the pairing, only the matched equipment set. Losing the ability to parry with a shield or second weapon is the normal cost of fighting with a claw in each hand.\n\nLore: The more iconic configuration: a claw on each hand rather than one claw and a bolt pistol or shield, a signature look for several assault-specialist Chapters in Black Library fiction and codex background, prized for the speed of a flurry of cuts over any single blow's power.\n\nDesign: Identical per-claw profile to the single Lightning Claw entry (paired weapons are the same item worn twice, not a mechanically different weapon), priced at $12,000, a discount of $1,000 on two single claws ($13,000) for buying the matched set. Making it a separate equipment entry (rather than a quantity of 2 on the single-claw entry) lets a character sheet show \"wielding a matched pair\" distinctly and lets the GM apply two-weapon fighting rules cleanly. Handling: total weight is two corrected 12 lb claws minus a small integration saving for the shared power-cell routing (22 lb rather than a flat 24 lb), not the doubled-wrong-number the old 3 lb entry would have given (6 lb for a \"pair\" of gauntlets meant to punch through Terminator plate was never plausible). Min ST (13), reach (C,1) and parry (-1) are identical per claw to the single Lightning Claw above, since each hand fights as its own weapon.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
