		{
			"id": "egTW1OZEqd6kVUe2A",
			"description": "Blessed Blade, Sororitas Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Mechanically an ordinary power sword; any anti-daemon or faith-linked combat bonus a specific consecrated blade carries in play is a character/relic trait, not a property of the weapon itself, and belongs in a traits file rather than here.\n\nLore: Adepta Sororitas power swords are frequently shown consecrated by an Order's chaplain before battle and treated as holy relics in their own right, especially those carried by Celestians, Palatines and Canonesses; the fiction does not suggest the blessing changes what the blade physically does to a target, only what it means to the wielder and her Order.\n\nDesign: Identical stat block to the Power Sword anchor entry (this is the framework's own instruction: a bolter built for the Astartes armoury and one carried by a Sister of Battle are the same weapon with the same numbers) at a higher cost reflecting the rarity and ceremony of a named, consecrated blade rather than any mechanical difference. Any distinct blessing/relic effect is deliberately left out of this equipment entry and left for a traits file to add on top, per the separation of concerns in data-format.md. Handling: identical to the human-scale Power Sword - weight 4 lb, min ST 10, parry 0 (Broadsword) - since a Sororitas Battle Sister is human-scale, not Astartes-scale, and this is the same physical blade.",
