					"attribute": "block",
					"amount": 2
				}
			],
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "eXgQuQx4sk5XqfPvY",
			"description": "Boarding Shield",
			"local_notes": "Larger and heavier than a combat shield, meant to cover a boarder advancing down a corridor or breach rather than a static line.\n\nLore: A large, heavy void-ship boarding shield used by Naval boarding parties and some Guard siege/storm-trooper formations clearing confined spaces where a bolter or lasgun can't easily be brought to bear at close range; background material treats it as a specialist, situational item rather than universal-issue.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Large Shield stats (DB 3, +3 Block attribute bonus) with a correspondingly higher min ST and weight than the Combat Shield; not anchored, built from Low-Tech shield-scaling logic. Handling: re-derived against Basic Set's actual Large Shield entry (B287: 25 lb, min ST 11, DB3) - min ST 11 already matched, but weight was previously set to 15 lb, a Medium Shield's figure paired with a Large Shield's DB. Corrected to weight 25, matching the real analogue.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
			"tech_level": "2",
