		},
		{
			"id": "esMAooLh5QKogV_yB",
			"description": "Storm Shield",
			"local_notes": "This entry is the physical shield only: the ceramite/adamantium plate, its bash attack, and its Block bonus. The storm shield's signature void/energy dispersion field - the part of its reputation that lets it stop power weapons, chainblades and even a bolt round outright - is a separate force-field feature layered on top and belongs in the personal armour file alongside other Astartes energy shielding, not here; treat this shield as \"just\" a very large, well-made Astartes plate until that feature is added from that file.\n\nLore: Carried by Astartes Terminators and some veteran assault troops (paired with a thunder hammer as the classic \"hammer and shield\" Terminator loadout); consistently shown stopping blows that would shear through lesser shields or armour, which the fiction attributes to an active energy field rather than the metal plate alone.\n\nDesign: Physical component built as an Astartes-scale large shield (Basic Set Large Shield DB 3, +3 Block) at Astartes weight and min ST, above the human Boarding Shield's figures the way the Astartes chainsword sits above the human one; the bash attack scales up accordingly (sw+1 cr, heavier plate than a boarding shield). The force-field component that does the real work in the fiction (per the framework's instruction that the force field is the armour agent's responsibility, referenced here only in notes) is deliberately left out of this equipment entry's damage/DR fields so the two files don't duplicate or contradict each other's numbers. Handling: re-derived from the human Large Shield analogue (25 lb, ST 11) the same way the Astartes chainsword scales from the human chainsword (roughly +8 lb, +5 ST) - 32 lb loaded and min ST 15, both well above the Boarding Shield's figures but not pushed as far as a solid ceramite slab would go, since a Terminator's storm shield is still carried and maneuvered in a fight, not just braced.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
